# Day X - Web Basics, HTML, JS & Security

## 1. How Website Works
- Browser sends a request to web server
- Request travels through the Internet
- Server processes the request
- Server sends response back
- Browser uses data to display webpage
 
## 2. Key Components of Websites

### Frontend (Client Side) 
- What user sees in browser 
- Responsible for:
  - UI (design, layout) 
  - Interaction (buttons, forms)   
- Built using:    
  - HTML
  - CSS
  - JavaScript

### Backend (Server Side) 
- Runs on server
- Responsible for:
  - Processing request
  - Handling logic
  - Sending responses

### Example Backend Tasks
- User authentication
- Database operations

## 3. Important Points
- Web server is a computer on the Internet
- Handles user requests
- Communication happens via HTTP/HTTPS
- Flow: Request → Process → Response

## 4. HTML (HyperText Markup Language)
- Used to build structure of webpages
- Works with:
  - HTML → Structure
  - CSS → Styling
  - JavaScript → Interactivity

## 5. Basic HTML Structure
- Standard format for every webpage
- <!DOCTYPE html> defines HTML5 document

### Main Tags
- <html> → Root element
- <head> → Contains metadata (title, etc.)
- <body> → Visible content of webpage

## 6. Common HTML Tags
- <h1> → Heading
- <p> → Paragraph
- <button> → Buttons
- <img> → Images
- <ul>, <li> → Lists

## 7. Attributes in HTML
- Provide extra information to tags

### Common Attributes
- class → Used for styling multiple elements
- id → Unique identifier for element
- src → Specifies image source

- Elements can have multiple attributes

## 8. Key Points
- HTML uses tags to structure content
- Only content inside <body> is visible
- id must be unique, class can be reused
- View source using Inspect / View Page Source

## 9. JavaScript (JS)
- Makes webpages interactive
- Without JS → pages are static
- Can update content in real time

### Usage
- Change styles
- Handle events (click, hover)
- Show animations

## 10. Adding JavaScript

### Inside HTML
- <script> </script>

### External File
- <script src="file.js"></script>

### Example
- document.getElementById("demo").innerHTML = "Hack the planet";

- Changes content of element with given id

## 11. Events
- Trigger JavaScript on user actions

### Examples
- onclick
- onhover

## 12. Sensitive Data Exposure
- Occurs when website exposes sensitive data
- Usually found in frontend code (HTML/JS)

### Causes
- Developer forgets to remove:
  - Login credentials
  - Hidden links
  - Sensitive data

### Where to Find
- View page source
- Check:
  - HTML
  - JS
  - Comments

### Impacts
- Login to application
- Access restricted areas
- Access backend configuration

## 13. HTML Injection
- Occurs when input is not sanitized
- Attacker injects HTML/JS into webpage

### Cause
- No input validation
- Input directly displayed on page

### How It Works
- User enters input
- Input used in JS to display on page
- No sanitization → executes as HTML/JS

### Example Flow
- User enters name
- JS displays: "Welcome + name"
- If input = <h2>Hacked</h2>
- It renders as HTML

## 14. Vulnerability
- User can control page content and behavior
- Can inject:
  - HTML
  - JavaScript

### Key Rule
- Never trust user input

## 15. Prevention
- Sanitize / validate all inputs
- Remove or escape:
  - HTML tags
  - Scripts
